.vercel

# node_modules is ignored wholesale, so a real `npm install` can never be
# committed -- the three/ stub inside it is force-added once (git add -f) and
# stays tracked from then on, because .gitignore never applies to a file that is
# already tracked. A negation like `!node_modules/three/**` would be wrong: it
# would re-include every file of a genuine three install too.
#
# Why the stub is committed at all: nine src/ modules do
# `import * as THREE from 'three'`, which the browser resolves through the
# import map in index.html. Node has no import map, so without the stub the
# whole dependency graph stops resolving the moment characters.js reaches
# voxel.js and every suite dies on an identical error. It lives in node_modules
# because that is the only place Node resolves a bare specifier.
node_modules/

# One-off CDP probe scripts, their screenshots and console captures. The
# harnesses worth keeping live in test/ and smoke-main.mjs; these were scratch
# work for a single audit and are kept local only.
.t1.txt
cdp-*.mjs
probe-*
match-*.txt
match-report.json
